  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the product\n$$ (\\tan 1^{\\circ})(\\tan 2^{\\circ})\\cdots(\\tan 88^{\\circ})(\\tan 89^{\\circ}). $$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$.\n\nPair complementary angles; each pair has product $1$, and $\\tan45^{\\circ}=1$.",
      "worked": "For each complementary pair,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\tan k^{\\circ}\\tan(90^{\\circ}-k^{\\circ}) &= \\tan k^{\\circ}\\cot k^{\\circ} \\\\\n\\tan k^{\\circ}\\tan(90^{\\circ}-k^{\\circ}) &= 1.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe factors form 44 such pairs, with $\\tan45^{\\circ}=1$ remaining. Therefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(\\tan1^{\\circ})(\\tan2^{\\circ})\\cdots(\\tan89^{\\circ}) &= 1^{44}\\times1 \\\\\n(\\tan1^{\\circ})(\\tan2^{\\circ})\\cdots(\\tan89^{\\circ}) &= 1.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
